# What a *client* wears to use this fleet — the Outfit you would have on your
# laptop, as opposed to node/Outfit, which is what each node serves.
#
# The difference that matters is the missing BASEURL. A node's Outfit pins its
# own local engine; a client's must not, because the whole point is that outfit
# picks a node and fills the address in. An Outfit that states one is taken at
# its word and never routed.
PROVIDER llamacpp
MODEL    org/fake-model
ALIAS    fake-model
CONTEXT  4096
FLEET    ../fleet.yaml
